      "lineNbr": 14346,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-09T08:49:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The comment in NetworkController says that we need to check the netId is the same:\n\n        // If this IP address is still assigned to another interface in the same network,\n        // then we don\u0027t need to destroy sockets on it because they are likely still valid.\n        // For now we do this only on VPNs.\n        // TODO: evaluate extending this to all network types.\n\n\nThe intent of the current code is to cover the case where a VPN does not disconnect, but changes interface with the same IP address.\n\nGenerally, sockets will only work on the netId they were established on. Just because two interfaces have the same IP address doesn\u0027t mean that sockets started on the old network will work on the new network.",
      "parentUuid": "eeb55726_f54b59f0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14346,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 14346,
        "endChar": 9
